# Critical env secrets (local → VPS → verify)

When the user asks to change / set / update / sync **any critical secret** below (or pastes a new value / says «обновил env»), do **all** of the following in one turn — do not stop at local `.env` only.

## Critical keys

| Key | Role | Verify (runtime container after recreate) |
|-----|------|---------------------------------------------|
| `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` | Bot API | `getMe` → 200 + expected username |
| `TWITCH_CLIENT_ID` | Helix / OAuth app | with secret: client_credentials → 200 |
| `TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET` | Helix / OAuth app | same; then Helix `GET /users?login=marfapr` → 200 |
| `TWITCH_CLIPS_REFRESH_TOKEN` | Create Clip (`clips:edit`) for video preview GIF | refresh_token grant → 200 + `clips:edit` in scope |
| `CLOUDCONVERT_API_KEY` | Clip MP4 → GIF | `GET https://api.cloudconvert.com/v2/users/me` → 200 |
| `DONATIONALERTS_CLIENT_ID` / `DONATIONALERTS_CLIENT_SECRET` | DonationAlerts OAuth | token endpoint or documented app credentials check → 200 |
| `TWITCH_EVENTSUB_SECRET` | EventSub HMAC | set non-empty if used; do not log value |
| `TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY` | Fernet for stored Twitch refresh tokens | non-empty if set; **rotating invalidates existing encrypted tokens** — warn user |
| `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` / `DATABASE_URL` | Bot DB (compose) | `docker compose … exec db pg_isready` / bot starts clean |
| `AIVEN_DATABASE_URL` | Cold DR mirror only | connect once; never treat as live bot DB |
| `POSTHOG_API_KEY` / `POSTHOG_API_KEY_PERSONAL` / `POSTHOG_ISSUE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Analytics / alerts | key present; no 401 on a cheap PostHog call if checking |
| `DEEPL_API_KEY` | Admin broadcast translate | cheap usage/auth call → 200 if checking |

Also treat as critical anything that authenticates a third party or encrypts user tokens. Prefer verifying the rows the user actually changed.

## 1. Local `.env`

- Set the key(s); never commit `.env`; never print full secrets (hashes / prefixes / lengths only).
- Reject placeholders (`your_…`, empty, Client ID pasted into a secret field).
- **Quote values** that contain `#`, spaces, or shell-special chars: `KEY="value-with-#hash"`. Docker Compose truncates unquoted `#…` as a comment.
- **Token-only values** — no trailing comments, scopes, or prose in the same value. Example: `TWITCH_CLIPS_REFRESH_TOKEN` must be the raw refresh token string alone (typical length ~30–50; if `split()` yields >1 part, strip junk and re-check).
- `TWITCH_CLIPS_REFRESH_TOKEN` must be issued for the **same** `TWITCH_CLIENT_ID` / `TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET` as prod, with scope **`clips:edit`**.

## 2. Prod VPS (immediately)

Host: `bot.themarfa.name` → `/opt/twitch-telegram-bot` (SSH: `VPS_SSH_KEY` / agent / `~/.ssh/artalk_vps` — same as [`vps-db-query.mdc`](vps-db-query.mdc)).

1. Update `/opt/twitch-telegram-bot/.env` for every changed key (same quoting rules).
2. Recreate bot so env is reloaded:
   `docker compose -f compose.vps.yml up -d --force-recreate bot`
3. If `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` changed, also recreate/update `db` per compose and confirm the bot still connects.

## 3. Verify (changed keys only)

Run checks against **runtime** container env (after recreate), not only the file on disk.

**Twitch Helix (client id/secret):**

1. `POST https://id.twitch.tv/oauth2/token` (`client_credentials`) → **200**
2. `GET https://api.twitch.tv/helix/users?login=marfapr` → **200** + user
3. Recent logs: no `401` / `403` / `invalid client` / `Twitch poll failed` for ~1 poll interval

**Clips + CloudConvert (video preview):**

1. Refresh grant with `TWITCH_CLIPS_REFRESH_TOKEN` → **200** and `clips:edit` in scope
2. CloudConvert `users/me` → **200**
3. Do not claim video-preview ready if either fails

**Telegram:** `getMe` with `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` → expected bot.

Report pass/fail briefly per checked key. If an auth endpoint fails, **do not** claim that integration is fixed.

## Do not

- Leave VPS on the old value after a successful local check
- Restart/recreate without rewriting `.env`
- Log access tokens, refresh tokens, API keys, or secret values
- Sync only a subset when the user updated several related keys (e.g. Twitch id+secret+clips refresh together)
- Put comments or extra words inside secret values
